        {
          "id": "10b",
          "label": "(b)",
          "text": "Using only the terms:\n• non-zero-digit\n• digit\n• letter\n• variable-identifier\ndraw a syntax diagram to show the definition of a variable identifier.\n\nreasonable effort has been made by the publisher (UCLES) to trace copyright holders, but if any items requiring clearance have unwittingly been included, the\npublisher will be pleased to make amends at the earliest possible opportunity.\nUniversity of Cambridge International Examinations is part of the Cambridge Assessment Group. Cambridge Assessment is the brand name of University of\nCambridge Local Examinations Syndicate (UCLES), which is itself a department of the University of Cambridge.",
          "marks": 4,
          "type": "name",
          "answerType": "short_answer",
          "hasDiagramRef": true,
          "diagramOnly": false,
          "parts": []
        }
      ],
      "marks": 7,
      "text": [
        "A variable identifier in a certain programming language is defined in BNF (Backus-Naur",
        "For",
        "form) as: Examiner's",
        "Use",
        "<non-zero-digit> ::= 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9",
        "<digit> ::= 0 | <non-zero-digit>",
        "<letter> ::= A | B | C | x | y | z",
        "<group> ::= <letter> | <letter><group>",
        "<variable-identifier> ::= <non-zero-digit><group><digit> | <non-zero-digit><group>"
      ]
    }
